# Vulnerabilities the image scan (.github/scripts/scan-image.sh) does not fail on. Empty is the goal.
#
# Only for a finding reviewed as not applicable to Chartmate (the vulnerable code is never reached, or the scanner
# misidentifies the package), never to get a release out past a real one: update the package or the base image
# instead. Each entry is one ID with an expiry date at most 90 days out, and the comment line directly above it
# says what was reviewed, by whom and why it does not apply (a test checks the format). Trivy reports the finding
# again once the date passes, so it gets reviewed again. Example:
#
#   # libfoo in the base image: only its CLI is affected, which Chartmate never runs. Reviewed by <name>, <date>.
#   CVE-2026-12345 exp:2026-12-31
